research program: Is there an influence on career choice? Pediatr Radiol 37: 876–878, 2007. 10.1007/s00247-007-0540-z [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 12. Erzurum VZ, Obermeyer RJ, Fecher A, Thyagarajan P, Tan P, Koler AK, Hirko MK, Rubin JR: What influences medical students’ choice of surgical careers. Surgery 128: 253–256, 2000. 10.1067/msy.2000.108214 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 13. Collins PB, Collins L, Darrow GB, Sepede J: Undergraduate knowledge of osteopathic medicine: What premedical students know about osteopathic medicine and its effect on burnout. J Am Osteopath Assoc 120: 855–864, 2020. 10.7556/jaoa.2020.149 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 14. Gold JA, Barg FK, Margo K: Undergraduate students’ perspectives on primary care. J Prim Care Community Health 5: 279–283, 2014. 10.1177/2150131914534072 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 15. Muncan B, Majumder N, Tudose N: From high school to hospital: How early exposure to healthcare affects adolescent career ideas. Int J Med Educ 7: 370–371, 2016. 10.5116/ijme.5801.f2cc [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 16. Liaw SY, Wu LT, Chow YL, Lim S, Tan KK: Career choice and perceptions of nursing among healthcare students in higher educational institutions. Nurse Educ Today 52: 66–72, 2017. 10.1016/j.nedt.2017.02.008 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 17. Danner OK, Lokko C, Mobley F, Dansby M, Maze M, Bradley B, Williams E, Matthews LR, Harrington E, Mack L, Clark C, Wilson K, Beech D, Heron S, Childs E: Hospital-based, multidisciplinary, youth mentoring and medical exposure program positively influences and reinforces health care career choice: “The Reach One Each One Program early Experience.” Am J Surg 213: 611–616, 2017. 10.1016/j.amjsurg.2016.12.002 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 18. Kane L: Medscape Physician Compensation Report, Medscape, 2019 https://www.medscape.com/sites/public/physician-comp/2019 19. Association of American Medical Colleges : US Medic