lointerstitial and cystic disorders (55%), CKD/kidney failure (55%), and AKI (56%) ( P = 0.02). Meanwhile, GPT-3.5''s response exhibited relatively higher concordance rate to questions in kidney transplant (86%), hypertension (84%), and CKD/kidney failure (82%) compared with the other six subfields: tubulointerstitial and cystic disorders (65%), pharmacology (70%), electrolyte and acid-base disorders (72%), AKI (74%), glomerular disease (75%), and kidney-related bone and stone disorders (76%) ( P = 0.03). Figure 2. Open in a new tab Accuracy of GPT-3.5 on test questions related to different nephrology subfields . Total accuracy (%) refers to the percentage of correct answers obtained by ChatGPT in either the first or second run. *Questions related to tubulointerstitial and cystic disorders and pharmacology are only present in Kidney Self-Assessment Program. #Electrolytes refers to the electrolytes and acid-base disorders. GD, glomerular disease; HTN, hypertension; KBSD, kidney-related bone and stone disorders; KT, kidney transplant; TICD, tubulointerstitial and cystic disorder. Performance of GPT-4 on Nephrology Test Questions GPT-4''s response to all nephrology questions had higher total accuracy rate compared with GPT-3.5 (74% versus 51% for GPT-4 and 3.5, respectively, P < 0.001) (Figure 3 A and Table 2 ). The total accuracy rate of GPT-4 was similar between the first and second run (68% versus 69% in the first and second run, respectively; P = 0.11). The GPT-4''s total accuracy rate ranged from 65% for glomerular disease, 70% for electrolyte and acid-base disorders, to 79% for AKI and kidney transplant questions. GPT-4''s response had higher total concordance rate than GPT-3.5 (83% versus 78% for GPT-4 and 3.5, respectively; P = 0.02) (Figure 3 B). GPT-4 provided higher concordance rate for correct answer ( P < 0.001) but lower concordance rate for incorrect answer ( P = 0.006) compared with GPT-3.5 (Figure 3 C). Figure 3. Open in a new tab Comparison of performance of GPT-3.5, GPT-4, and nephrology examinees on nephrology test questions from Nephrology Self-Assessment Program and Kidney Self-Assessment Program. (A) Total accuracy (%) refers to the percentage of correct answers obtained by ChatGPT in either the first or second run. The average score (%) is obtained from nephrology examinees, including nephrologists and nephrology trainees. (B) Total concordance (%) refers to the percentage of identical answers provided by ChatGPT between both runs by comparing the results with those of the initial run, regardless of their correctness. (C) Concordance (%) of correct and incorrect answers compared with the first run. Statistical significance was assessed using (A and B) the McNemar test and (C) Chi-squared test. Table 2. Performance of GPT-4 on nephrology test questions and by different nephrology subfields Questions by Subfields Nephrology Self-Assessment Program Kidney Self-Assessment Program Overall Correct Incorrect Correct Incorrect Correct Incorrect Nephrology questions, No. 508 467 975 1st run, No. (%) 373 (73) 135 (27) 286 (61) 181 (39) 659 (68) 316 (32) 2nd run, No. (%) 374 (74) 134 (26) 302 (65) 165 (35) 676 (69) 299 (31) Concordance between 2 runs, No. (%) 354 (95) 100 (74) 256 (90) 102 (56) 610 (93) 202 (64) Total concordance, No. (%) 454 (89) 358 (77) 812 (83) Total accuracy, No. (%) 393 (77) 332 (71) 725 (74) Glomerular disease, No. 90 33 123 1st run, No. (%) 56 (62) 34 (38) 23 (70) 10 (30) 79 (64) 44 (36) 2nd run, No. (%) 53 (59) 37 (41) 22 (67) 11 (33) 75 (61) 48 (39) Concordance between 2 runs, No. (%) 53 (95) 29 (85) 21 (91) 9 (90) 74 (94) 38 (86) Total concordance, No. (%) 82 (91) 30 (91) 112 (91) Total accuracy, No. (%) 56 (62) 24 (73) 80 (65) Hypertension, No. 60 42 102 1st run, No. (%) 48 (80) 12 (20) 24 (57) 18 (43) 72 (71) 30 (29) 2nd run, No. (%) 50 (83) 10 (17) 27 (64) 15 (36) 77 (75) 25 (25) Concordance between 2 runs, No. (%) 47 (98) 9 (75) 23 (96) 11 (61) 70 (97) 20 (67) Total concordance, No. (%