g the effectiveness of Envarsus in Kidney Transplant Recipients in an evidence based fashion with the ultimate goal of publication - Honorarium deferred; 3. Exam Item writer for ABIM—no Honorarium; 4. Region 3 UNOS living donor physician representation on the UNOS Living Donor Committee—no Honorarium; 5. ASN Transplant Workforce Member; 6. ASN CET Workgroup; and Other Interests or Relationships: Unsure so declaring all these: American Society of Transplantation (AST): Board Liaison to the Living Donor Community of Practice; AST Transplant Community and Community Education Committee; Incoming Chair of Planning Committee, AST Cutting Edge in Transplantation Planning Committee (CeOT)2022; Member, AST Community Education Committee; UNOS Region 3 Representative to OPTN Living Donor Community; Schwartz Center Rounds for compassionate Rounds—Facilitator. N. Leca reports Consultancy: Eurofins TGI; and Research Funding: Angion, CareDx, CSL Behring, Hansa, Memo, Natera, Novartis, Transplant Genomics, and Verici. S. Mehta reports Research Funding: CareDx and Natera/Prospera. S. Mohan reports Consultancy: HSAG, Sanofi, and Specialist Direct; Patents or Royalties: Columbia University; Advisory or Leadership Role: Chair, UNOS, Data advisory committee; Deputy Editor, Kidney International Reports (ISN); Member, ASN Quality committee; Member, SRTR Review Committee; and National Faculty Chair, ETCLC; and Other Interests or Relationships: Research Funding from Kidney Transplant Collaborative and NIH (NIDDK, NIHMD and NIBIB). S. Ong reports Honoraria: Horizon Therapeutics. S. Parajuli reports Research Funding: CareDx and Veloxis Pharmaceuticals; and Advisory or Leadership Role: CareDx, Eurofin, and Horizon Pharmaceuticals. R. Parsons reports Ownership Interest: AAPL, AMZN, BAC, CRM, CSCO, DIS, MSFT, PG, SO, and VZ; Research Funding: Hansa Biopharma AB, Natera, Regeneron Pharmaceuticals, Inc., and Transplant Genomics, Inc.; and Other Interests or Relationships: American Association of Kidney Patients, American Society of Transplantation, American Society of Transplant Surgeons, and National Kidney Foundation. L. Preczewski reports Consultancy: None under the ineligible definition—all unrelated to health care. Specifically Boston Proper Brands, Levenger, Publix Supermarkets, and Varsity Brands; Ownership Interest: None under the ineligible definition—all unrelated to health care. Specifically Banc of California, Berkshire-Hathaway, PacWest Bank, and Rivian; and Advisory or Leadership Role: American Society of Transplantation, Jackson Health System, and Northwestern University. M. Samaniego reports Advisory or Leadership Role: American Society of Transplantation—Fellowship Committee—Chair and American Society of Transplantation—Kidney Pancreas Community of Practice—Executive committee member. R.D. Santos reports Ownership Interest: Pfizer; Research Funding: CareDx, Merck, and Veloxis; Honoraria: UpToDate; Advisory or Leadership Role: AST Transplant Nephrology Fellowship Training Accreditation Program Board of Managers Chair, unpaid; and Other Interests or Relationships: AST Transplant Nephrology Fellowship Training Accreditation Program review committee; Advisory group meeting for Horizon. D. Sawinski reports Ownership Interest: CareDx; Research Funding: National Institutes of Health; Patents or Royalties: UpToDate; Advisory or Leadership Role: American Journal of Kidney Diseases , American Society of Transplantation Board of Directors, Clinical Transplantation , and Councilor at Large; and Other Interests or Relationships: UNOS Kidney Committee member; Expert witness testimony. N. Singh reports Research Funding: CareDx and Transplant Genomics; Honoraria: Mallinckrodt, Natera, and Veloxis; Advisory or Leadership Role: AST KPCOP Chair—no payment and OPTN Pancreas Committee Member—no payment; and Speakers Bureau: Mallinckrodt, Natera, and Veloxis Pharmaceutics. V.S. Sridhar Other Interests or Relationships: Conference and travel support from Merck Canada. A. Wiseman reports Employer: AdventHealth Transplant Institute; Consultancy: Hansa, Medeor, Nephrosant, Sanofi, Talaris, Transplant Genomics, and Veloxis; and Speakers Bureau: Sanofi, Takeda, Transplant Genomics, and Veloxis. C. Zayas reports Advisory or Leadership Role: AST COP Renal and Pancreas Program, AST COP Transplant Administrators, AST Transplant Nephrology Accreditation Committee, and Baylor Transplant Islet Cell Program Safety Monitoring Board; and Other Interests or Relationships: AST, Emory Transplant Center, Life Link Foundation, Medical College of Georgia, Southeastern Transplant Coalition, and UNOS. All remaining authors have nothing to disclose. Funding None. Author Contributions Conceptualization: Prince M. Anand, Gaurav Gupta, Neeraj Singh. Data curation: Neeraj Singh. Supervision: Neeraj Singh. Validation: Neeraj Singh. Visualization: Neeraj Singh. Writing – original draft: Prince M. Anand, Roy Bloom, Gaurav Gupta, Neeraj Singh, Bekir Tanriover. Writing – review & editing: Deborah Adey, Enver Akalin, Prince M. Anand, Roy Bloom, Diane Cibrik, Beatrice P. Concepcion, Darshana Dadhania, Rowena Delos Santos, Mona Doshi, Oren Fix, John Friedewald, Gaurav Gupta, Mallika Gupta, Syed Ali Husain, Vineeta Kumar, Nicolae Leca, Shikha Mehta, Sumit Mohan, Angie Nishio Lucar, Song Ong, Sandesh Parajuli, Ronald Parsons, Luke Preczewski, Millie Samaniego, Deirdre Sawinski, Saed Shawar, Neeraj Singh, Karim Soliman, Vikas Srinivasan Sridhar, Bekir Tanriover, Alexander Wiseman, Mareena Zachariah, Carlos Zayas. References 1. Concepcion BP, Alasfar S, Levea S-L, Singh P, Wiseman A. The transplant nephrology workforce in the United States: current state and future directions. Adv Chronic Kidney Dis. 2020;27(4):336–343.e1. doi: 10.1053/j.ackd.2020.05.005 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 2. C Wiseman A Akalin E M Dadhania D, et al. Defining the roles and responsibilities of the kidney transplant medical director: a necessary step for future training, mentoring